        <p>3 o'clock. G. Newton (C.A.) 5, J. Haywood (C.) 6. J..Watkine (K.Q.) 4y A. Hogan (R.) 7. J. 111-nnigan (R.M.) 6, H. Lawton (C.) 5. H. Houghton (G.) 7, W. Cartel: (R.) 5. G. Gibson (R.M.) 6, -0.-Cliffe (C.) 6. R. Callon (P.T.) 5, R-Alrimelow (C.) 6. J. Heywood (W.) 7, H. Cook (C.) 2. H. Langlej (R.) 3, A. Waiting (C.) 6.</p>
        <p>A. Gilbert (G.) 6, P. Burgess (W.T.) 6. J. Cooper (C.A.) 4, A. Ellison (MIL) 4.. P. Cohen (RM.) 7; W. Potter (C.) 6. G. Caddick. son. P. &amp; K:) 4, W. Shave (P.T.) 4. W. Masse; (RM.) 7, J. Gleave (C.) G. Evans (C.) 6, S. Milner, jun. (W.) 6. D. Robinson (C.) 6, J. Campbell (R.) .6. A. B. Boardman (C.H.) 5, J. Woods, jun. (R.) 6.</p>
        <p>.3.40. , R. Smith" (C.A.) 6, S. Shave, jun. (W.T.) 7. W. Dwerryhouse (W.T.) 6, E. Malligan (N.) 7. E. Jones (M.H.) 6, A. Maskill (R.) 5. H. Denim (W.C.) 3, A. Brauthall (R.) 6. W. Hatton (C.) 7, M. Cunningham (F.S.T.) 5. J.W. Plinskin (C.C.) ,a; J, Cunningham (F.S.T.) 6 F. Littlewood (C.) 5, B. Green (C.) 4. G. Postlethwaite (F.S.T.) 5, W. Harrison (R.) 7.</p>
        <p>4 o'clock. E. Rowlands (C.A.) 8, Ike Holcroft (C.) 5. H. Worsley (R.) 5, George Hatton -(W.C.) 4. T. Boardman (W.) 6, D. Elwell (C.) 7. J. Stanley. (L.C.) 5, P. Tatlovic- tey 7. A. Bowyer (P.T.) 4, M. Tavlin (C.) 6. H. Houghton (R.) 5, R., Haigh- kR.) 5. H. Ilankey (C.) 5, W. Bridge (CL.) 4. E. Harper (C.A.) 4, Arthur Savage (F.S.T.) 7.</p>
        <p>4.20. J. Stafford (C.H.) 4, J. Lowe (R.) 4. R. Poole (C.) 7, W. Currie (G. 13. 7. A. Foster (W.C.) 6, J. Lester (R.) 5. H. Daniels (C.) 6, A. S. -Watkins (R.) 6. J. Middleton (C.) 4, E. Millington (R.) 7. W. Patrick (G.) 3, W. Rowlands (G. 8. 6. •G. Ward (L.W.) 6, W. Mulholland (C.A.) 4. G. Lowe (R.) 4, R. Williamson (G.H.C.) 4.</p>
        <p>ABBREVIATIONS.—A.A., Assurance Agents; Armitage and Rigby's; C., Crosfields; Conservative Club; CA. County. Asylum; C.L., Cheshire Lines; F., Fletcher's; F.M., Firth Mattress; F.S.T., Fennel-street Tannery; G., Greening's; G.T.; Grappenhall Tannery; G.8.T., Guest Bros.' Tannery; H.T., Howley Tannery; L.W., Longford Wire; L.C., Liberal Club; M.H., Monks, Hall; N., Naylor's; ON., Orford Tannery; P.P., Plumbers and Painters; P. &amp; K., Pearson and Knowles; P.T., Penketh Tannery; R., Rylands's; R.M., Richmond's; R.8.T., Randall Bros.' Tannery; W., Walker's; W.R., Wire Ropery; W.T., Warrington Tan- nery; W.C., Whitecross; 8.H., Bull's Head; C.a. Cemetery Hotel; S.H.C., St. Helens Cable; 8.G., Bowling Green. Officials: J. Willett, F. Dean and J. Howarth.</p>
