      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-05-06_WidnesExaminer_art0200" n="art0200">
        <head>AMOMI4MMINI</head>
        <p>AMOMI4MMINI</p>
        <p>FOOTBALL.</p>
        <p>RUGBY.</p>
        <p>NORTHERN UNION.</p>
        <p>HOW THEY STAND.</p>
        <p>Dewsbury And Leeds Tie For ' First Position In League.</p>
        <p>Northern Union football -was brought to a close for the season on Saturday, when, as a result of the matches, Dewsbury and Leeds tie for the first position. The latter team secured an easy victory at home over Hull, while Dews- bury, away from home, accounted for, Hull Kingston Rovers. Wigan were only beaten by a goal at Huddersfield, while Leigh again beat St. Helens Recs., for the third time in four games. Results z-r- Leigh, 8 points; St. Helens Recs., 0. St. Helens, 5; Swinton, 3. Salford, 23; Broughton Rangers, 3. ' Leeds, 24; Hull,- 6.- '- Huddersfield, 10; Wigan, 8. Oldham, 12; Rochdale Hornets, 2. Dewsbury, 9; Hull Kingston Rovers, 5. Hunslet, 16; Halifax, 5.</p>
        <p>RESULTS TO DATE.</p>
        <p>Points. Per</p>
