      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-05-06_WidnesExaminer_art0239" n="art0239">
        <head>Medic Al.</head>
        <p>Medic Al.</p>
        <p>FITLLY-TRAINED NURSES for private work —medical, surgical, maternity, fever.—Nurses' Association, 139. Withington-road, 'Whalley Range, ‘1 anchester. Tel. 19 Chorlton.</p>
        <p>UDIES.—Mrs. W. Wood, Medical Specialist n all Female Ailments, Irregularities, Anemia, eta. Do not waste time or money experimenting with unknown remedies when "Challenge Remedy" will cure you. Price 2s. 9d., 4s, Eld. Advice free.— Mr. and Mrs. W. Wood. 20. Louis-street. Leeds.</p>
        <p>IJADIES. --Nurse Hammond's Improved Remedies act in a few hours when all else fails. Surprisinaly effective. Send stamped en- velope for FREE SAMPLE to E. C. Hammond, 304, High Holborn, London. WHY STAMMER? Particulars free.—Write The Charlesworth Co., "Speech Specialists," 47, Sankey-street, Warrington.</p>
        <p>"MEW BRIGHTON. Comfortable homely 11 Apartments. 8 minutes Ferry ; 2/- night 2 persons.—Mayes, 1. Windsor-street.</p>
