        <p>PRIVATE JOHN VARLEY. Died of Wounds.</p>
        <p>vious to the above message, ran :—" I am sorry to say that your son has been wounded in the side, leg and chest. He is now a little easier, but very weak. He sends his love to all at home?' Private Varley, who was 21 years of age, was employed at the Vulcan Foundry before enlist- ing, which he did immediately upon the out- break of war. He was educated at St. Alban's Day School, King-street, and was a member of the Catholic Young Men's Society.</p>
        <p>WOUNDED. LANCE-eORPORA I. J. PEARSON. Shrapnel Wounds In The Head While In The Trenches. Mr. Pearson, a widow, 11, Derby-road, Stock- ton Reath, has been informed that her eldest son, Lance-Corporal John Pearson, of the Border Regiment, has been wounded. A comrade sent the news, but details are, as yet, lacking. Lance-Corporal Pearson, who is 28 years of age, was,. before enlisting, employed at the</p>
