        <p>BOWLING ASSOCIATION. Draw For The First Round Of Club Championship. The chief business transacted at the council 'meeting of the Warrington and District Bowling Association, held at the King and Queen Hotel on Tuesday evening, was the draw for the first round of the club championship, to be played on May 20th and May 27th. Thirteen entries were received for the championship, and the draw resulted as follows: Conservative Club Juniors v. Rylands's No. 2. Rylands's No. 1 V. Houghton's. King and Queen v. Conservative Club Seniors. Walton v. Earlestown Vulcan. Bull's Head v. Bank Quay. • Byes: Cemetery, Conservative Club, Latch- ford; Whitecross. Start at 3.30 p.m. • It was agreed that all matches during the season should commence at 3.30 p.m. After that hour teams to arrange mutually. Messrs. Houghton's Wire Works Club made application for affiliation to the Association, and the club were accepted. The council decided that the handicap fixed for July Bth, 15th and 22nd should be called "The War Fund Handicap." A. GLEAVE IN FORM. A. Gleave, \Roebuck (5) was successful 'in the first, second and third rounds of the Easter Handicap played off in the qualifying sections of the Lancashire County Amateur Association last Saturday at Lower Broughton. Some people never have a show becauie they are always waiting for free passes.</p>
